# The weapon in the glove (#385.10, research #453): with the custom, forearm or hands model the held weapon is
# placed from the glove's hilt frame (the handle centre on the grip axis inside the closed fingers), never from the
# hidden Arx hand, the blade's edge toward the knuckles; with `arms arx` the weapon keeps today's placement.
# PROPOSED status.json keys (385.10 implements them):
#   vr.weapon.frame           = glove | arx          which frame the weapon is placed from
#   vr.weapon.hiltToGrip      units, handle anchor to the glove's grip axis point (~0)
#   vr.weapon.edgeToKnuckles  degrees, the blade's edge axis vs the glove's knuckle direction
#   vr.weapon.anchor          the anchor's distance from the pommel along the handle, units (per class table)
#   vr.weapon.tilt            the sword's forward tilt in degrees: 0 | -15 | -30   (cfg vr_sword_tilt, `grip tilt <deg>`)
# The right hand holds the sword (mvp-items). The pose numbers are a first guess: move the POSE, never the assertions.
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 weapon-in-glove
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence weapon-in-glove -Save mvp-items
@sim idle
@save mvp-items
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
# The custom arms: a test-only model since #466 (classic is the default) until #486 removes it
arms custom
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.active eq true
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq custom
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true

# 1. The custom glove: the weapon is drawn from the glove's frame, the handle in the closed fingers, the edge to the knuckles
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq glove
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToGrip lt 0.5
@assert vr.weapon.edgeToKnuckles lt 5
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq 0
@assert vr.weapon.anchor gt 0
@shot glove-default

# 2. The same raised to the face, the hand turned (the roll is pinned, not left to the controller)
vr-sim hand right pos 0.12 -0.1 -0.35
vr-sim hand right rot 0 90 0
vr-sim head rot 0 -15 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq glove
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToGrip lt 0.5
@assert vr.weapon.edgeToKnuckles lt 5
@shot glove-raised

# 3. A hand past the reach (as arm-fit.xrs's far pose): the arm stretches at most 10%, the weapon stays in the glove
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
vr-sim hand left off
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -1.5
vr-sim hand right rot 0 0 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.right.custom.stretch gt 0
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq glove
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToGrip lt 0.5
@assert vr.weapon.edgeToKnuckles lt 5
@shot glove-far
vr-sim hand left on
vr-sim hand right pos 0.2 -0.3 -0.35
@frames 20

# 4. The forearm and the hands models take the same frame
arms forearm
@frames 10
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq glove
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToGrip lt 0.5
@assert vr.weapon.edgeToKnuckles lt 5
arms hands
@frames 10
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq glove
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToGrip lt 0.5
arms custom
@frames 10

# 5. The tilt switch: -15 leans the blade (angle changes), the status follows, the weapon stays in the glove
@remember angle0 vr.weapon.bladeAngle
grip tilt -15
@frames 15
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq -15
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle gt {angle0+10}
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle lt {angle0+20}
@assert vr.weapon.hiltToGrip lt 0.5
@assert vr.weapon.edgeToKnuckles lt 5
@shot tilt-15
grip tilt -30
@frames 15
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq -30
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle gt {angle0+25}
@shot tilt-30
grip tilt 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.weapon.tilt eq 0
@assert vr.weapon.bladeAngle lt {angle0+2}

# 6. A value off the table is refused or snapped to a variant - never stored as is
grip tilt 40
@frames 5
@assert vr.weapon.tilt le 0
@assert vr.weapon.tilt ge -30
grip tilt 0
@frames 5

# 7. The Arx hands: the weapon keeps today's placement (the hidden hand's)
arms arx
@frames 15
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq arx
@assert vr.weapon.inHand eq true
@shot arx-model
arms custom
@frames 15
@assert vr.weapon.frame eq glove

@assert errors eq 0
